# mix-of-capabilities 12×09 — la catena delle cause, percorsa nel verso detto e
# resa per passi, sui fatti causali della KB viva (e sulle cause insegnate
# parlando: burning fossil fuels causes pollution). Mai un «No» per una catena
# non trovata.
[mock live]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test a two-step chain is followed and said]
!timeout 30
> does rain make surfaces slippery?
< Yes: rain causes wet ground, and wet ground causes slippery surfaces.

[test a three-step chain through a taught cause]
!timeout 30
> does burning fossil fuels cause rising seas?
< Yes: burning fossil fuels causes pollution, and pollution causes climate change, and climate change causes rising seas.

[test the chain is not walked backwards]
!timeout 30
> do slippery surfaces cause rain?
<! Yes:

[test the polar causal form walks a mediated chain instead of stopping at the missing direct cause]
!reset
!timeout 30
> does pollution cause rising seas?
<~ Yes: pollution causes climate change, and climate change causes rising seas.
<! nothing I hold says
# §25.5 (l3-upgrade.md): la stessa lettura sbagliata oggi si dice con la cipolla composta
<! no fact I hold decides whether
> does rain cause wet ground?
<~ Yes
> does rising seas cause pollution?
<! Yes
